\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{commit}{6e11455}
\import{base-macros}

\p{The launcher has one option for warm measurements. \code{\verb~|-X passes=N~} with \code{\verb~|passes-mode=reload~}, the default, makes a complete run per pass, load included, which is what the metric asks for: after warm-up, with loading pipelined with checking. \code{\verb~|passes-mode=recheck~} delegates to the driver's check-only passes. Both modes print one line per pass with wall, CPU, collector, load and check times, units, workers and memory; the exit status is that of pass 1, and a later pass with another verdict is reported as a disagreement and declined. A run with one pass takes the unchanged code path, which a test compares for an accepted, a rejected and a declined export. \code{\verb~|bench/warm.sh~} turns the pass lines into table rows. Published with 43 tests.}

\p{Detail: \src{rlvm-main/README.md}, \src{bench/README.md}. Commit \commit{6e11455}. Session: [machine speed and pipeline](ses-CVTE). Related: [the metric is warm wall clock](dec-7QMU), [the launchers](design-launchers).}
